=========================================================================================================
13_scaffold_split.py — Performance under scaffold-grouped outer folds
=========================================================================================================

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Random folds put close analogs of the same chemical series in both the training and the test
  part, which can make a         model look better than it would be on a new series. Steps SC01
  and SC09 repeated the benchmark with folds that keep every         Bemis-Murcko scaffold in a
  single fold, for the Morgan stacking ensemble and for the default D-MPNN. This step puts the
  two results next to the random-fold results, and tests the network against the classical
  ensemble on the shared         scaffold folds. The scaffold results are expected to be lower;
  the question is whether the comparison changes.
